- **The first pole stays verbatim wherever it is quoted** (#43): ch60's recall of it reads "a stamp renewed four times", identical to ch7. The protected-text audit's "two renewals on paper" substitution inside the quoted pole was reverted by the coordinator; non-protected counts still say "two renewals on paper". If the owner chooses #43 option (b) "renewed twice", it changes in BOTH ch7:225 and ch60:253.
- **The book's last line and the six restored units** (Gault's last note; the personnel query; the waystation board; "You couldn't read me…"; Cael's reply to Daeva; the closing exchange) are verbatim from the protected wording, with only the edition's mandatory changes ("Since my Kindling"; "Nine fragments"; the personnel query's teaching-assistant role, calendar and house frame).
- **The shelf is the SECOND camp beyond the Line and the first fire** — Book 7's plan is amended to match (audit fix 16), not Book 6.

## 47. Book 6 ch49 — the certification minute's "evaluator of record" (coordinator ruling, 2026-10-11)
The protected Tier B minute reads "*Evaluation-protocol certification: declined by the evaluator of record; proceeding on the presiding seat's authority.*" In this edition Gault is the evaluator of record and the Archmarshal's office is the certifying office that declined. **Ruling: the protected line stays verbatim and is read as the form's own mislabel** — an old column heading with no place for the right office — which the scene already dramatizes (four pens stop; Gault "had declined nothing"). One plain sentence was added outside the protected line so a young reader is told so directly: "The refusal was the Archmarshal's; the form's old column had only Gault's title to put it under." Owner may instead release the protected line and have it name the certifying office.

## 48. Book 7 reconciliation to edition Book 6 (coordinator defaults, 2026-10-11)
Source: `book-07-void-roads/state/B6-RECONCILIATION-AUDIT.md`, `B6-RECONCILIATION-F-RERUN.md` (Sol) and `B6-RECONCILIATION-COORDINATOR-OVERRIDES.md`. Defaults in force until the owner rules:
