+2. First six: `Karis could not light the lamp.`  
+   Last six: `and it was nearly a laugh.`  
+   Listening notes: Lane A speech join ruled sound. Before: `"Yes." She thought about it. "It's a different hurt from the ankle. That one was a thing I'd done, and this is only a thing that's there."` After: `"Karis turned thirty animals with a page she'd not tested," said Lira presently.` Both halves belong to Lira, and the second is explicitly tagged; no listener will invent a speaker change.
+3. First six: `It rained on the seventy-ninth day,`  
+   Last six: `Lira. "It keeps my mind off."`  
+   Listening notes: Seln's route report is introduced as a report and remains attributable. Clean.
+4. First six: `It was Lira who knew first,`  
+   Last six: `as I can hold the pencil."`  
+   Listening notes: Oryn's entrance gives her role and name before the longer treatment scene; the unnamed `woman` cannot be confused with another speaker. `crossbow` ends in BOH. Clean.
+5. First six: `She took off the second slate,`  
+   Last six: `and put the stocking on again.`  
+   Listening notes: restored protected unit ruled sound. Before: `"All of them. That's what I pay. It doesn't come from nowhere."` Protected sentence: `Lira's face went a colour that was not white, and she said "Cold," not to anyone, and then "No. It's going along," and put her head back and shut her eyes.` After: `"That's right," said Oryn. "Lie still and let it."` The bodily sensation, patient, and healer remain explicit.
+6. First six: `She ate before she touched anybody`  
+   Last six: `wasn't," said Lira, who had been.`  
+   Listening notes: Oryn owns the clinical questions; Karis's faint answers and Lira's final denial are tagged. `close loaf` is KLOHS. Clean.
+7. First six: `She came to Cael when the`  
+   Last six: `turned palm upward on her knees.`  
