editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:21:> - **Accounts/open threads:** start day 100 with 108 in hand; the Fallow hundred remains unpaid in Pike's box; one sixty-yard four-strand rope, two HOLD slips and three replies remain owed; the completion report travels west saying six; seven hounds remain untracked north/south along the outside (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:19,247-251`; `manuscript/chapter-33.md:193-195`; `manuscript/chapter-34.md:273-307`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:499-505`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:22:> - **Relationships/knowledge:** Lira still owns “Later” and knows Cael chose not to declare while her arm was held; the other four know the same mechanism, while Oryn knows only that he made the hill effects and that something changed during the reading (`manuscript/chapter-31.md:229-235`; `manuscript/chapter-33.md:243-277`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:216-244`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:24:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — the telling and its cost (Reader Standard), binding.]** Movement 5 ends with Cael having taken the tenth fragment in Oryn's long reading without telling her first, and telling her the minute it was over. The edition treats that as a wrong done knowingly; the companions named it so and he agreed. This movement's first scene must therefore give Oryn full agency: SHE names what was done to her, in her own terms; she establishes whether and how the taking touched her; and she sets conditions and a cost that Cael cannot pay in advance out of his own ledger (the plan's "self first, ask first, tell her" is HER condition, stated by her, not offered by him). He does not argue his reasons, is not forgiven on the page for having confessed, and consent is not supplied after the fact. The acquisition stands and is not undone. Sources are told to her by Path, not by person, except the three she has touched; Seln is not identified as the source of Shadow-adjacent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:34:Minute twenty-one on a plank table in Thornwater's back room. Ten fragments. A healer who has just felt something change in a patient she cannot read, and who has been told she is about to hear what he is.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:40:- **The telling on the table** is explicitly a retelling to Oryn of what Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln already established in edition B6: his own Arbiter woke at Kindling; the station plate lit eleven seconds late; the failed-safe word replaced the old name; the Arbiter then went dark. Sources are named by Path, not by person, except the three Oryn has touched. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B4, B7] The notice said aloud. The page fetched from the loft and read twice in its counted places. **Her answer** (protected): "So I couldn't read you because…" … "Then use it on yourself first. Before anyone… I want to be the one you tell." Oryn's new condition governs Tide reading outward: self first, then ask first every time. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B4] "You're the colour of the wall…"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:41:- **The cascade: it listens, it doesn't pull (three nights).** His own current at the edge of every thought; the nine coming up out of it one at a time and told apart by sound; "a room he had lived in for eighteen years with the lights suddenly on." Brom on the ladder ("How many people." / "Nine. Ten. I can't hear the tenth. It's the thing I'm hearing with." / the forge story). Day two: **Storm heard resettling** in the yard, a hand on the well's rim; the ground arriving half a beat late under a counted foot, so he **relearns the Wind economy in the yard** while the listening runs (a learning encounter). **Oryn's "Where is it loudest."** "Here… It's not louder there. It's nearer." Ask first, said in the yard: "I ask the dying." / "I ask first. Every time."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:43:- **The birthday (day 102):** Lira instigates one-armed, pays one-handed, and has been practising the pouch for a week without saying so. Brom acquires three kinds ("Three."). Six places in the common room. Oryn at the table "like a woman who has sat at a great many tables and stayed at none of them." **The line written** (protected). "A stop. Good. Write it down before it changes." **Pike's Fallow copy** arrives by carter: “Six went in. Six came out.” It lands against Cael's memory of Gault's last line, *The instruments will not see its like.* Gault's physical leaf remains in the west with the withdrawal file and is not among the party's papers. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit D5, N5] Hesk's package does not come, and the absence sits at the table unremarked. Seln: "He's counted her… So has the broker." The apples argument, which Karis loses on the merits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:45:- **The week of tables (days 103–109).** The ring laid flat (eleven sheets one numbered rubbing to each upright, each upright's height recorded [corrected at M4 close]); the tally of *kinds* she will not number from one site. **Five findings, each a scene:** (1) *the Quieting*: grammar for a process, not a place; (2) **identical failure** across five sigils (Iron R1, Copper, Iron R3 [corrected at M6 audit: Karis retains Iron Rank Three], Bronze, Iron R4; Lira's clock in Lira's words), and the looms sentence, unfiled (protected); Seln's "Six… I'm counting it." and the struck six; (3) **the strata as a physical demonstration** (four chips oldest to the right; the knife marked and the floor didn't; no stroke, no join, no laid edge; weathering past the founding stone), with **[UNBOUND] once** (protected), then Brom's "Say it with less."; (4) **the stakes, once, in four sentences**; (5) **the observation entered and the interpretation stopped**: "It's a fear." / "Does it help?" / "It's just correct." Oryn works the hold in the yard (nine late here, eleven at the next) and looks at the table once.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:46:- **New, a learning arc: Lira and the bowman.** The bowman off the gate-walk (unnamed) teaches her to shoot braced one-armed, against a rail and a knee, with the steading's bow spanned for her because she cannot span one-armed and says so. Short sessions, his few words, her fierce economy. This plants the Hall (M8). Oryn's order is kept exactly: the left arm holds nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:47:- **C2, staged:** Oryn decides to leave her mule with the crew. Three boxes and a girl with one arm need it more than a healer whose holds keep beasts. She will take the next hold's beast at Millrace. Her decision, said in her register.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:48:- **Day 110.** Lira first at the gate-walk at dusk, in the order he has had for fifteen days (protected exchange); the fighter's question ("It felt like a Third-day."); her hand along the plank to his boot; "Then six." **The circle of six**: what each of the four saw, in order; Karis's five findings said; Seln's "Yet."; Oryn's "I'm not going to guess past it."; nobody puts a verb between the facts; the four wheres; "We find the others…"; "One at a time, for money." Oryn: "North in the morning… Don't go in without me…"; her hand on Seln's shoulder. **Brom at the ladder** ("It's a count. You like counts."). **The Vastin window** (three sentences). **Oryn at the well**: the rule written while she watches (protected); "Once is a morning" (the debt's terms set by her: three readings on different days, then all of it at once); "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."; the note written under the rule. **The second pole** in the log (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:49:- **Oryn's window north (111–112):** the spare rope, the road bending, what she carries in her head. It ends before Millrace.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:55:- The debt to Oryn (telling her the self-reading) is **owed**, with the day set by her. It is not paid in M6.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:63:The sensation-language of listening, kept to sensation; Thornwater in the hard-cold days [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] (ice on the trough, the grain going up the ladder past where they sleep); the tables' daily rhythm; the bowman's manner and words; the birthday's warmth and humor; the shape of each finding scene; all the windows.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:67:Dawn on the 111th: Oryn north on a route seventeen days late at Oxhollow, carrying a spare rope; the crew with her mule, three boxes and a hundred and two in hand. A rule on the page and a debt with a date. Ten fragments and one place that doesn't move. "Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three." The completion report has been on a desk somewhere for eight days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. The miller, Millrace's ford-keeper and patients, the six on the rim, the second Anchor specialist, the hide-woman, the crew of three and Teague's crew stay unnamed. **No faces on the rim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈35,400. **Seln cutaway ≈2,200** (night of day 112, after the council: the two slips laid side by side in his head; twelve years carrying the case for people he cannot see [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B6]; why he wants a face; he may not open the case or decode anything). **Teague cutaway ≈2,400** (days 113–115: at Millrace, the five not back; the walk south to look; the rim's ground read in lantern light, the crossbows, "declaring"; holding the rim at dawn without being asked; no crew names).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:10:- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈40 per 10k. ≈17 growth beats. Supporting beats for all six, plus Pike and Teague.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:14:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — still-place continuity (Sol plan audit, Movement 6), binding.]** ‘The still place’ is an established private log label in locked Books 5–6, not a new phrase in Movement 8. Movement 7 must not spend the new beat: keep Cael’s finding private, unnamed aloud, and owed to Oryn. In Movement 8, the beat is that the old log label becomes a repeatedly read LOCATION and a shared spoken finding: after the second and third self-readings, Cael attaches ‘the still place’ to the located anomaly, tells Oryn while reading her with permission, and she answers the finding. Do not present the words as newly coined or new to the reader; preserve ‘Not the Quiet. Not a fragment.’ and all withheld-source limits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:16:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — Oryn's circuit and Millrace (EXC-B7-003, owner-resolved 2026-09-04; do not reopen), binding.]** Oryn left Thornwater by the northern wicket at first light on the 111th saying, in the protected words, "North in the morning… I'll be three days north by the time you're back at the board… Thornwater's on my route." Millrace is one day SOUTH of Lowmarch on the Stair road, and she is at her table there on the 113th. The owner's ruling is that both stand: her circuit brings her round to the Stair-road stop within three days (the track from the northern wicket bends west and then south, as ch44 shows). Do not contradict either. Let it be true on the page in one plain line when the five find her at Millrace (for example which stop she cut or sent word to, as the packet's "word sent up the route" already allows); do not have anyone remark that she said north.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:20:> Movement 7’s packet already carries the day-111 start, Oryn gone, mule with the crew, Lira two weeks into the order, and the report west (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:20`). It must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:22:> - **Cael:** nineteen; ten fragments; deployment thirteen; Shadow still only once; the eleven Wind leans are practice; the tenth has read only himself, once; two further self-readings on different days and the whole telling to Oryn remain owed; he may read nobody merely to test the ability; Oryn’s answer and remaining price stay withheld (`manuscript/chapter-39.md:245`; `chapter-40.md:189–211,319–385`; `chapter-44.md:167–209`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:24:> - **Equipment and money:** 102 marks in hand; three boxes and Oryn’s mule; Seln’s shut case; Oryn’s empty pannier left on the saddle while she carries the other and the spare rope; the yard crossbow, belt hook and five bolts travel with Brom; the ring sheets, bark slips, four chips, calfskin rings and charcoal round remain in Karis’s boxes (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:55–67,379`; `chapter-41.md:3–39`; `chapter-42.md:205–277`; `chapter-43.md:171–215`; `chapter-44.md:209–245`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:25:> - **Knowledge:** all six know Cael functioned inside the Ring and know that his self-reading found something, but none except Cael knows what; Oryn knows the mechanism but not that Seln supplied Shadow; Karis’s hypothesis is neither spoken nor entered; the Quieting name and five findings are shared; nobody has put a verb between the facts (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:11–105,113–117`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:27:> - **Open accounts:** Pike has eight completed lines but the crew has not heard the eighth read at the board; the Fallow hundred remains in Pike’s box, the ferryman’s rope and two HOLD slips remain unresolved, Hesk’s parcel has not arrived, three letters are unanswered, and seven hounds remain untracked (`manuscript/chapter-40.md:221–263,383`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:173–179`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:28:> - **Oryn:** day 112 closes just short of the mill; she is sixteen late out of Thornwater and seventeen late at Oxhollow, has left the mule, and has not forgiven Cael or received the self-reading (`manuscript/chapter-44.md:223–301`). Her exact location on day 113 is Millrace under M7, subject to the protected north conflict (`packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:30`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:36:First light on the 111th at Thornwater: Oryn gone north, her mule with the crew. Lira is two weeks into the season's order. A completion report sits on a desk west of the Line.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:42:- **Thornwater → Lowmarch (111–112), the first cold.** The fourth honest catalogue from the rise.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:43:- **Pike says the Fallow line before the door is shut;** it costs a line (eleventh; "Teague's ten up"). Then what the wall cannot say: thirty years, forty-odd crews, nobody over a line and back, "Six in and six out, and the sixth a healer." **The room updates** without a word (the hide-woman, the crew of three gone grey, the carter from the first week, the boy). **Teague stands** when they come in and sits at "eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:44:- **The second slip** on the nail of read-and-returned (protected text). Pike, unasked: "Nothing else ever… I'd not take it." Karis: "That's the carter's second circle." **Seln's anatomy** (protected lines): registry prose; the same clerk; a size, not a wage; a floor he *knows*; "pre-restriction inventory"; "The boy's the price of the case."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:45:- **The council, the second honest collision:** Lira for walking away (the fence at forty and the walk at fifty, and pace the third circle on their own time); Brom ("Three hundred's a number a man doesn't reach for." — his father and the horse); Karis ("I would go alone."); **Seln: "Take it… People have faces. Six years I've wanted a face."** [OWNER-pending #50] Cael's sentence to the whole table (protected), then why: the assumption is wrong and cannot be known to be wrong. **Brom quotes Rooke**, the first person he has ever quoted: "Doors open both ways… I don't like it. I'm in." Lira: "I want it entered that I said walk away." The log (EXC-B7-002). Pike marks HOLD unasked and says it to the room. **Teague at the door** (protected): "If you're late back, we'll come look." / "Noted.", the first *Noted* to anyone above them on the wall.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:46:- **Millrace (day 113):** the wheel heard before the roofs; the ford-keeper's "Five off the ridge" / "I know." **Oryn's table**: fifteen, three serious (a crushed hand, a child's chest, an old woman's knee with a ladder in it) and a dozen small with one hand each. **Ask first, refused** ("You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next."), entered first. Karis: "She was curious about you. Enter that somewhere." **Her arithmetic aloud**, finger by finger. "You're asking me to break the route." / "I'm not asking. I'm telling you where we'll be." / "That's worse. That's a healer's sentence." "I'm not going to be anybody's sixth." **Word sent up the route** by carter (late, how late, why, where to send for the child). **Terms** (protected). Lira's sixth-chair line. The fork log.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:49:- **Day 114, the trap (≈9,000–10,500 across two chapters).** The crossing in Seln's order. **The bolt at forty-five yards** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]: "Ridge." Six hooded on the rim in road grey (two south, two east, one west, one north). **The Anchor course** closing the line behind them; Cael sees it with perception only. Bolts skip off the fused plate. **Lira runs *down***, and the unit follows. **Forty steps.** The chamber, ten strides square, its ceiling the floor; walls carved; at the middle "something cased… a cord," unread. **The doorway**: "They can shoot the bowl… They can't shoot the stair." **Oryn without hands**: lamp, eyes, two fingers; "Tape it. Leave the bolt."; "the bolt's the plug"; "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." Lira's mend reopened on the stair wall. **The stalemate, given room**: the square of grey going white and grey; a bolt sent down to stop at the thirty-first step; Brom grey and not worse; Karis with her back to the wall she would give a year to read. The design read aloud ("It thinks the floor did the same thing to all six of us."). **The order:** up alone with the one he was given. Oryn: "Ask first." / "I'm not reading anyone." / "I know. I'm saying the rule out loud so it's been said on this floor too." Lira: "Later." **The ascent, Shadow alone**, across the bowl unseen; the rim scanning for a shout that cannot exist. Once Cael is within ten feet of the knot, Anchor perception finds it; he then makes the separate purposeful unbinding, without assigning that action a measured reach, rate or price [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B1]: **the knot found and released**, the course going slack like rigging. **Over the stone, declaring**: Wind, Storm seeding the rut, Compression at contact, Ember held out. He removes one man from the plan and does not fight him. The rim breaks as professionals break. The west one looks back for a second, hood up, nothing in it. Four crossbows left; no faces. "Back."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:50:- **Out at dark:** "There. Back… The clock started again." The bolt-head cut and the shaft drawn; an hour on Brom; a quarter on Lira ("It held a stair…"). His bill: the suite spent on a week's rest. **Seln breaks a stock across the stone**: "No faces." The log (protected). **Teague's crew at full dark** (protected exchange); he does not ask how.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:51:- **Day 115:** Teague holds the rim unasked ("We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted"). **C3: Karis paces the Stair's perimeter in the morning** with Lira one-armed on the line, under four rim-holders who are theirs, and gets two hundred. **Down with two lamps**: the air at the twentieth step; the chamber catalogued properly; Oryn's "What are they" / "Lines." **The kit**: open, contents in taking-out order, the cord laid toward the east wall, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar beside its mallet, point bright, the floor unmarked (EXC-B7-004: "Twice, by the head… Nothing goes into this."). **The ledger read by Seln**: distances, the radius in their own hand, a designation in an index he does not know, and the last line, *third site confirmed on bearing* —. **Karis's body at "bearing."** Six hours; twenty-nine sheets; "Sheet"; Lira ahead of her every time; **forty-one** (protected); the line *between* the courses at the radius; "A measurement is a fact about a ruler…" **The kit carried up**: Brom refuses help three times. The rim-holders: the spear grounded once. The log at the stone (protected). The straightedge out on the carter's map, not yet touching anything.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:56:- **The rim saw a practitioner walk out declaring, and saw nothing work inside.** Teague saw the same and asks nothing.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:59:- Oryn joins as a stop on her route, never as "sixth," never "join." The Stair slip's three hundred is taken and never paid.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:60:- Teague's crew is unnamed, including in Teague's window. The healer of no Path does not appear until M8.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:64:The Lowmarch room; Millrace's texture; Oryn's patients; the road lesson's sensation; the chamber's cold; the stalemate's small human business; the ascent's suspense inside the planted rules; the rim action's choreography; the six hours; both windows.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. Oxhollow's ford-keeper, the smith, the patients at Oxhollow's table and Teague's crew stay unnamed. Of Oryn's seven holds, only Oxhollow and Thornwater are named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈34,200. **Lira cutaway ≈1,800** (day 78, the ledge: the burst her body chose before she did; "That was me. The loud thing."). **Oryn cutaway ≈2,600** (days 84–92: out of Oxhollow's gate north on her route, the carter's hand she owed, the child three stops on, the patient she wants to read whole; she decides to put a day on the route; it ends before Thornwater). **Teague cutaway ≈1,400** (day 84, Oxhollow's ford at dusk: four sentences priced before he says them).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:10:- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈78 per 10k (Tide taught in full; the herd's derived sense; tiers). ≈17 growth beats. Supporting beats for Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Oryn, Teague, Pike.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:14:> Movement 3 already carries the day-70 injury snapshot, fifty-two in hand, Teague out on two holds, the unmended ankle, and deployment count one (`packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:16-18,35-42`). Its author must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:16:> - The stillhound finding in Cael's hand and its Lira-hand archive copy: discharge sense; slight sight/hearing used for station and testing; water mask; first-mover following; learning. The 110 yards and dusk remain unexplained; two hounds remain open downstream (`manuscript/chapter-11.md:357-401`; `manuscript/chapter-12.md:153-171`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:18:> - The ford is clear, the lip-stone row is whole, and Thornwater now knows the five as the crew from its ford (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:197-227`; `manuscript/chapter-13.md:53-63`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:19:> - Karis holds a new *This side* leaf, the carter's map bend two days east of Thornwater, and the wife's three-sentence quiet-ground rumor in the middle box with *everybody knows* underlined twice. Nobody has asked what it is (`manuscript/chapter-12.md:153-175,295-357`; `manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-445`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:21:> - Board/account state beyond the packet's purse figure: six earned lines, 62 earned total, twelfth of thirteen, Teague eleven up; Pike has set a bare tack for the incoming unnamed ford slip (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-465`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:23:> - Personal residue: Cael has stopped counting Lira's runs; Lira's “what am I becoming” remains unanswered in the log; Brom keeps Pike's six-word answer against his skin; Karis can hold a pencil but her palms still hurt (`manuscript/chapter-13.md:183-219,291-337`; `manuscript/chapter-14.md:361-443`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:27:**Read before drafting:** B7 source `chapter-05.md`, `chapter-06.md`, `chapter-07.md`; `BOOK_MAP.md` §5 (Oryn and Teague windows), §7 (Tide), §8 (stampede), §10, §12 C7–C8; `STATE_LEDGER.md` (Movement 2 append).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:31:The seventieth morning, at the plank. The calf is a leg on the flat and says nine uphill. Brom's wrist is closed and must not pull. Lira's ankle is taped and stiff. Karis's palms are two pink lines each. Fifty-two in hand. Teague's crew is out on two hold slips.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:37:- **The Oxhollow slip** (seventy, on the map, paid at Oxhollow) sorts itself to the top, and he counts why: it pays; nobody's finger is on it; it is *ground*. Pike: take a cart ("You want to tell a ford it holds a cart, you'd better have had one on it."). Seln asks about shale-backs quietly at the plank's end, and Cael does not go to listen. The smith's cart is six against its return. The boxes go because there is nowhere to leave them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:43:- **Day 80, Oryn**, introduced through her walk and then her hands: "Who's worst?"; the set ("That's the part you'll mind"); the mend in less than an hour (Lira: "Cold… No. It's going along."); she sits as a carter sets down a known load; "That's one."; "Hands on. That's the only way it works… And I can't do it to me."; Brom's wrist ("Then it should have closed in a month and hasn't, because you've pulled on it."); Karis: "Ember. And nothing. You're empty."; "Hm." at the lattice line. **The first failed surface reading** on Cael: she stops in the middle, looks at her hands, tries again, and her face does the instrument's thing. The protected exchange ends on "That's a *finding*."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:45:- **Oxhollow (day 84):** the table under the lean-to, hers twenty days at a time; worst first; "That's three." The map paid seventy ("Then they go round."). **The second and third readings** (ribs knitting with "nothing doing it"; the wrist and neck, nothing wrong, still nothing): "a river in the dark." **The two readings taught before they are load-bearing** (surface: a count of ten; deep: both hands, minutes, still and whole, at a mending's cost; "I don't run it on a road"). If the stall is named (C8 default: at most once), it is a limit she prices and hates, never used. **Three questions** (right places — yes; faster; no healer ever got anything — no). "That's the visit." He has a sentence asking her south and does not say it. "Thornwater's on my route in nine days… I want to read you when you're not broken." / "Nine days."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:46:- **Teague at Oxhollow's ford at dusk:** four lines (protected), not unkind; Cael has no argument. The log. The image: Teague's four walking the ford quiet, and a mule a mile up the north road with a woman on its down-slope side.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:51:- Oryn knows nothing of fragments; no deep reading is run. She records nothing and remembers. Her Tide in full: contact only; about three serious mendings a day, fed and slept (two on a road); cannot heal herself; "cannot mend what I can't read."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:54:- Nobody mentions quiet ground. Oryn's other five holds are not named, here or in her window.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:55:- Teague learns nothing he couldn't read off a yard.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:59:The bench's days and weather; the herd's look and sound; the exact choreography inside the planted geometry (fin, split, cart, boxes); Oryn's first look at each of them; the walk down; the yard at Oxhollow; which patients come to the table; Lira's and Oryn's windows; humor (Brom's "Carrying." / "Not pulling."; Lira on a mule not mentioning the mule).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:63:Day 84: a hundred and sixteen in hand, six owed to the smith for a cart in a gorge. Three ribs taped, a calf bound in her cloth, a leg that is new, an ankle taped, a wrist mended and not to pull. Three failed readings, and a healer who wants a fourth "when you're not broken." Thornwater in nine days. Two people out here are measuring him, and neither has a seal.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:9:- Owner names: canon only. Do not name the courier, carters, ferryman, smith, landing broker or his clerk, the steading's woman, the bowman, the crew captains on the wall, or anyone in Teague's crew.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:10:- POV: Cael ≈30,700. **Seln cutaway ≈1,800** (days 10–40: walking every road out of Lowmarch, and later out of Thornwater, alone, first, unasked; the report nobody asks for). **Teague cutaway ≈1,500** (day 49, the door: his three counted before the job, then the board, then the five; he finds Seln on the second pass). Teague's crew is never named, including in his head.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:11:- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈82 per 10k (the book's teaching peak: the board, the hold, the nine as held things, tiers at the plank). ≈14 protagonist growth beats. Supporting beats for Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Pike, the carter, Teague.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:26:- **OWNER #23 / C1 (binding):** in Lowmarch's first week the horse and cart are sold. A horse is fodder and a sign that says *paper*; the scrub ruts past Lowmarch take mules. The sale and remaining Book 6 purse become the sealed reserve; the board purse alone is “in hand.” [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit N7] Give it one good scene and an argument with a joke in it, then let it go.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:27:- **Lowmarch, day 9, and the board read like the Cinder House board.** Fourteen slips, not one pricing the crew. Pike: sixties, one arm, "Copper, Force, thirty years on the roads." "Walk, carry, climb, fight." / "In that order?" / "Depends on the day." A heading opened with five names and five columns: Job, Hirer, Witness, Outcome, Price. No tier column. He reads it upside down and looks for the missing column "the way you look for a stair in the dark, with a foot."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:30:- **The Thornwater road (days 41–43), ≈4,000:** the carter at the fire ("Two carts went quiet on it last month"); the stretch at dusk after a wheel cost an hour; positions; the valley's noise; **Lira's hand up at a hole in the noise**; Seln without turning, "Don't declare anything." / "Walk. Same pace."; "I could clear it." / "No." / "I know. I'm saying it so I've said it."; Brom becoming exactly as large as his body and no larger; Karis deciding five times not to take out the notebook; the five items (keeps station at forty-five yards; makes no sound; tracks the buckle; won't cross the gravel fan; reacts to nothing because they gave it nothing); it stops a hundred and ten yards short of the fence. No blow struck. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; this line also keeps the generic "last month" per coordinator O4]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:31:- **Thornwater:** the gate, the woman with the lantern, the bowman who doesn't point; "First crew I've hired that knew to shut up."; "Stillhound… You shut up. It went home."; "You're paper." / "Yes." / "Hm."; the slip marked; the grain loft; six days; the carter back on the fourth; Pike's copied line; the log with "Note the date. Season's open, and for once it isn't theirs."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:32:- **Lowmarch, day 49 — the board anatomized:** a woman captain's line read before and after; the eleven-bale captain ("Say it again and I'll write it"); "The book's for me. The saying's for them."; the wall at the lower inn; "A Bronze who lost my carter…"; "Did you ever hear of a ledger-keeper called Vell?" / "No."; Seln's finger on the carter's map, the asset-restriction **said once and put away**, the map turned east. "Four lines. Nobody lost, nobody hurt, nobody knows you." Brom: "Eleven."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:34:- **Teague across the sill:** he counts his three before the room. He reads Lira from her feet, Brom as a fact, Karis with the beginning of a smile, and Seln on the second pass. Cael reads him back, item by item. Neither speaks. The last of the day lies across the sheet: one word at the top, five names at the bottom, eleven lines of light between.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:40:- The stillhound's sense is **unknown** in this movement. Karis has the word, not the mechanism; the discharge finding belongs to M2. Nobody hears the words *quiet ground*. No healer, no Tide practitioner, no Oryn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:42:- Teague and Cael exchange no words. The Thornwater carter is never named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:47:Chapter boundaries; how much of the skip stays in log-voice; the meadow's life (tents turning over, the ash and the carter with two mules); the three contracts' small problems; the courier's face; Pike's ink-pot and stone; how Seln's window walks a road; the humor (Lira and the board, Brom and animals, Karis underlining). Which scene the C1 sale lands in.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:51:Day 49: thirteenth of thirteen, with eleven lines between them and Teague. "I'm free. First time." Something out here hunts Paths, and nobody has given them the reason. Teague has read them and been read. The ford clearance, forty marks, sits on the plank with HOLD and his name beside it, and his crew is going out on the cold road for a week. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. Teague's crew (including the older healer of no Path), the hide carter, the ferryman and his boy, the old woman at Thornwater, the carters at the fire and the inn's keeper stay unnamed. **The fourth site stays unnamed.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈29,900. **Teague cutaway ≈1,700** (days 117–120: following the crew's trail three days along a bearing he does not understand, the healer brought because a shoulder was mended once; sitting down beside the boy; the column). **Karis cutaway ≈2,000** (days 119–120 at the far fire: three copies, the ledger, the edge laid and moved; it ends exactly on the pencil stopping; no who or why). **Seln cutaway ≈1,600** (days 124–128, the road home: the ledger in his coat; giving it to Karis and not asking for it back). **Oryn cutaway ≈2,800** (day 122 to about 128: the gap north-west, four days, three weeks late; Thornwater; the old woman's knee; writing the letter, ending on its four lines).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:10:- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈55 per 10k (the still place, the inventory, the map). ≈17 growth beats. Supporting beats for all six, plus Teague, Pike and Teague's healer.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:12:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — still-place continuity (Sol plan audit, Movement 6), binding.]** ‘The still place’ is an established private log label in locked Books 5–6, not a new phrase in Movement 8. Movement 7 must not spend the new beat: keep Cael’s finding private, unnamed aloud, and owed to Oryn. In Movement 8, the beat is that the old log label becomes a repeatedly read LOCATION and a shared spoken finding: after the second and third self-readings, Cael attaches ‘the still place’ to the located anomaly, tells Oryn while reading her with permission, and she answers the finding. Do not present the words as newly coined or new to the reader; preserve ‘Not the Quiet. Not a fragment.’ and all withheld-source limits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:16:> Movement 8's packet already carries the day-115 rim, bearing, two mules, six people, Brom mended once, Lira closed again and Teague turning back (`MOVEMENT-008.md:18–20`). Its author must additionally inherit these surviving-prose facts:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:18:> - **Cael and the debt:** nineteen; ten fragments; deployment twenty-three; Shadow has now been used exactly twice and is closed for the rest of the book; Tide has read Oryn once by leave but Cael has still read himself only once. Two self-readings on different days and the full telling remain owed, Oryn's day remains hers, and neither her withheld answer nor forgiveness has been supplied (48:229–235,273–279; 51:197–225; 52:355–359).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:19:> - **Bills and bodies:** Cael's right forearm bends but carries Compression's blow, and his left palm is taped with an unmended weal; Lira's reopened marks are shut and the sling is shorter, but the no-hold order and taped/unmended ankle stand; Brom's right arm is bound after one shoulder mending and must not be used until Oryn says (51:123–163; 52:5,75).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:20:> - **Equipment:** Brom has Oryn's bow, hook and five unshot bolts; the four captured crossbows are disabled and their thirteen bolts do not fit it. There are three archive boxes, the crew's brown mule, Oryn's grey jenny, 102 marks, the recovered kit, and Seln's shut case (51:167–197; 52:303–359).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:22:> - **Knowledge limits:** the index, stroke-and-bar and last unfinished entry remain uninterpreted; Karis's hypothesis remains unspoken and unentered; nobody has theorized why Cael works inside; Oryn still does not know Seln supplied Shadow; Teague knows only that one practitioner walked out declaring (50:181–213; 51:239–257; 52:169–213).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:23:> - **Open accounts:** the three hundred is taken and never to be paid; Pike's Fallow hundred, the ferryman's rope, Hesk's parcel and three replies remain outstanding; Teague forfeited the four-mark weir job and still has a day's fence posts (51:263–325; 52:355–359).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:24:> - **Oryn's route:** she leaves Movement 7 nineteen days late at the oxen ford, “or more,” with word sent north about where she is and where to send if the child's breathing changes; she remains a stop on her route, never a sixth or a joiner (47:133–229; 48:273–279).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:25:> - **Other people:** the six faceless attackers are gone with no attributable identity; Teague's three and every member of the rim remain unnamed; the healer of no Path has not appeared (51:91–103,263–383).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:29:**Read before drafting:** B7 source `chapter-21.md`, `chapter-22.md`, `chapter-23.md`, `chapter-24.md`; Book 8 `chapter-01.md` (the exit seam); `BOOK_MAP.md` §1 (ending, binding), §7 (the still place named; Teague not read), §8 (Hall allowance), §10 (Ch21–24, the closing exact), §11 (fourth site; instruments true in his hand), §12 C3, C6; `STATE_LEDGER.md` (Movement 7 append).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:33:The Stair's rim on the 115th, with a bearing taken off two sites with a brass edge. Brom's shoulder is mended once, and Lira's arm is closed again. Six people and two mules. Teague's crew is turning back toward Millrace.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:40:- **The Drowned Hall from the rise:** roofless, twelve strides square, a spring through the broken floor, a marsh exactly as wide as the Quiet. "Third." **The line** at the marsh's edge ("Gone"/"Back"); **stake thirty-three** (old, and no second); mud **heaved from below** along the water's edge ("It's never been out."); a bar at the hall's lip **bent from below**, read from a hundred and eighty-five yards. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] **Oryn's lore**: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:42:- **Day 119, the Hall (≈5,000–6,000):** Brom *stops* to put Karis up the wall and the floor opens under him; he puts her up before he goes sideways. "Get *off* the floor." **The coping** as cover and trap. Karis copying the wall she kneels on, funny for exactly one exchange. **Brom's shoulder opens**; he slips on the wrong wall. **Oryn into the water, skipping**, the healer reaching a falling patient (not heroic, only nearest). **The second pass turns** toward where she is going. **Cael in, declaring:** Compression takes the strike into a standing frame at the broken edge; **Anchor laid on the floor** at the broken centre. "A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest." It surfaces whole for the first time in anyone's memory. "Brom. Wall. Your weight. Now." **Four bolts into the pale**: Lira twice, braced one-armed against the coping and a knee, with Seln spanning between (the bowman's lessons pay); Seln twice. The point released; the jaws close on water; it lets go and goes down, alive. "Walls… Twelve sheets." It is left there.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:43:- **Costs at the track's end:** Oryn's hour, "Twice…" (protected); the long sit, wet to the waist; his bill (Compression in the ribs, Anchor held against biting, the read at its dearest under water). **The exchange** (protected) ending "Lie still. I want to read you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:44:- **Two days at the marsh (119–120):** two fires. Seln's blanket over Karis's shoulders. Lira keeps the bolt in the bow. Brom: "Twice." / "Twice." Oryn sleeps in front of people. **The second self-reading** (an hour; the banks a limit; **the still place**, named here for the first time; the river round a stone it has always known; four things he can count; protected log). The third before dawn: "the same." **Oryn changes the order**: "You in me." Asked and granted; surface, then a minute of the long one at her count, and while he is in, **he tells her exactly**; her finding (protected); "Write it down and stop touching it." **C3: Karis lays the cord at the Hall's perimeter** in the marsh between copies. **Teague's crew** along the track with a fifth: the older healer of no Path, "Twice?" / "Then it wants binding, not hands." The two women bind it. **Teague sits down beside him**, as Brom once did. "What are you." **The wrist a foot from his hand:** not the short reading, not the long one, not the asking. "Why did you stop reporting?" (protected exchange). "The board's going to need a new column." The log (protected). **The pencil stopping** at the far fire.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:46:- **The walk (121–122):** frost that rings; one cart of hides and a lifted hand; holds shut; the six catalogued because they will be five; the first night in a ruined hold's lee ("Twice." / "Twice." / "And not three."). **The fork:** "three weeks late there… I'm going back to being the route." He walks her fifty paces and does not ask. "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." **The four behind him, with one mule.** The log at the fork (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:49:- **Lowmarch (129–131):** the fifth honest catalogue, from the landing. **The season line read** (protected); the ledger turned toward him; **no number**; "too small" (protected); the room's "Eleventh." / "Aye." **Teague's term** and "Noted." The healer's single look at Brom's shoulder. **The cold-term fence** given over ("Ours.") [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]. Karis takes the back room and pays without counting (ninety-six). **The inventory** (protected; the audio rule). **The last ferry**: nine pieces sorted aloud; **Hesk's straightedge** with the note (protected); the replies west (protected). **Oryn's letter by carter** the morning after (protected): "Six, by letter." "She'll say when." / "After the thaw." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48] **The map**: four circles, the bearing, both edges laid along it, **touching the three paced centres for Cael exactly as for Karis**. "The sites were on an alignment. Not random." "Someone made this pattern." Four seconds. **The closing, exact.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:55:- **Teague is not read** and learns nothing of the mechanism. His crew is never named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:58:- Lira's order stands at first snow (Oryn "will say when"). The ankle is unmended. Brom's shoulder is bound, not mended a third time. Oryn's crossbow is with Lira, with one bolt left.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:64:The bearing's country; the Hall's water and stone; the fight's moment-to-moment inside the taught rule; the marsh's two days; Teague's manner beside the fire; the walk's last mild days [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2]; the crest at dusk; the road home into snow; the inn by lamp; every window.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:68:Book 8 Ch1: Lowmarch with the ice coming and the ferry's ropes taken in. Ninety-six in hand. A kit on a table. A map with a line going off its edge. A healer at Thornwater with a route and an arm to release. A captain's after-thaw term. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] A fourth circle twice the size behind a fence of iron. And a question asked once at a table that nobody answered.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. The hide-woman, the landing broker's clerk, the smith, the Thornwater people and Teague's crew stay unnamed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈35,400. **Teague cutaway ≈1,200** (day 89: reading the Fallow slip twice, putting it back, telling Pike he knew; his instinct that it is wrong, without a reason). **Karis cutaway ≈1,400** (night of day 95 at the stone: writing a stride, not a hypothesis; the line felt in her own sigil).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:10:- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈50 per 10k (the line's mechanics as trials: Arbiter, sigil, declaration, render). ≈18 growth beats. Supporting beats for all five, plus Oryn, Pike, Teague, Ephram, Vell.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:12:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — the Quiet line and OWNER-pending #49 (#49 default in force), binding.]** The protected log entries for this movement stay WORD FOR WORD, including "Mine didn't. Mine's been stopped since I was fourteen.", "Everyone's Path dies at the line and mine didn't", "Mine has been asleep since I was fourteen" and "because whatever I am isn't a Path". They are Cael's own log shorthand, and his fourth entry says so himself. Everything OUTSIDE the protected lines carries the edition's canon exactly: at the line the five live Arbiters (Karis's, Lira's, Brom's, Seln's, Oryn's) stop, at the same step; Cael's own Arbiter woke at his Kindling and has been dark ever since, so nothing in him changes at the line; and his fragments go on answering inside it. Narration and dialogue never say "his Path" or "Cael's Path", never say his Arbiter is awake, working or unaffected, and never explain WHY the fragments still answer. Do not paraphrase a protected entry in narration in a way that repeats its loose wording as fact. The owner may later release these lines; write so that nothing else would need to change.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:16:> Movement 4 already carries the dusk-of-84 location, 116 in hand / six owed, taped ribs, bound calf, new leg, missing right boot, Oryn north, Teague south, nine days to Thornwater, and the three boxes (`packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:18-20`). It must additionally inherit:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:18:> - The protected shale-back finding remains **derived, not tested** after an uncontrolled two-cause event; twenty-five are seen on day 81, while the missing five remain “heard, not sworn” (`manuscript/chapter-17.md:235-251`; `manuscript/chapter-19.md:195-203`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:111-113,341-343`; fix 5).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:20:> - Karis spent nine points/eight channels for eight seconds and is empty; on day 80 Oryn barred even a spark for one week. She could write one line on day 82 and hold the purse on day 84, but that does not release the restriction (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:41-53,279-301`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:215-219,359-361`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:22:> - Cael's three left-low ribs were broken day 78 and received five bands on day 81, to be lifted on day 99 by Oryn if possible; his reopened calf is only cloth-bound. His nine fragments are held, Shadow remains sealed, and deployment since the Line is one (`manuscript/chapter-19.md:121-155`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:3-45`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:325-333`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:23:> - Oryn has failed three surface readings of Cael, knows only that he heals fast with no readable current, knows nothing of fragments, has run no deep reading, keeps no written record, and has put one day on her route for the promised whole-and-still reading (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:317-351`; `manuscript/chapter-22.md:53-89,137-155,211-233`). Her mule still carries her panniers and covered crossbow; do not spend owner decision #24 early (`manuscript/chapter-20.md:143-159`; `OWNER-DECISIONS.md:103-107`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:24:> - After fixes 6–9, Teague knows only what his own schedule and the yard/keeper show: he missed Oryn on day 81; on day 84 the five have no cart, have healer-made bindings, delivered a paid no, and all survived. He does not know they caused Oryn's lateness and knows nothing of fragments or the mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:237-295`; fixes 6–9).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:25:> - The three boxes are whole at Oxhollow; the reserve is sealed in the third. The marked Oxhollow slip must return to Pike. The long map leaf was paid for on the keeper's board; the keeper is its buyer. Seln's closed case remains on its strap, and Hesk's satchel still carries the log, old volume, notebook, Hesk letter, and Pike's bark lines (`manuscript/chapter-15.md:153`; `manuscript/chapter-20.md:27-37,89-93`; `manuscript/chapter-21.md:321-361`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:323-327`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:27:> - Pike's board has not yet heard the traverse: six lines, twelfth of thirteen, Teague eleven up remain the last spoken standings until the marked slip reaches Lowmarch (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-465`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:174-176`). Hesk's letter is still unanswered, Lira's earlier question remains unanswered, and two stillhounds remain open downstream (`manuscript/chapter-14.md:439-451`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:329-331`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:35:Oxhollow's bank at dusk on the 84th: a hundred and sixteen in hand, and six owed. Ribs taped, the calf bound, Lira's leg new and her right boot gone. Oryn is walking north; Teague's crew has crossed south. Nine days to Thornwater.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:41:- **Six days Oxhollow → Lowmarch (days 84–90), lightly on the page:** the ford walked quiet a day behind Teague's crew; Lira's carter's boot for two marks, packed with linen; the tape hated by noon; Brom keeps the healer's week to the hour and picks up the middle box with both hands on the eighth morning. A small physical problem on the road is optional and the author's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:42:- **Lowmarch, day 90:** two hold slips with HOLD and **five names** ("Holds came to the ferry. Asked who. I said you."), waiting a fortnight or Teague. The traverse line read and priced: "Sixty-four's what the job was worth." / "Fair." **The posting under the stone's far edge**, the dust-curve on it, the hook-and-bar seal in wax; he reads it upside down, then gives it to Pike. Pike's face stops; Cael counts nine. "That's the Fallow Ring." / "That's quiet ground." **Pike's speech** (protected) and "You'll know. Your Arbiter tells you. It stops." Karis brings the page with two lines under it from the middle box: "A location. And a contract." The smith paid: a hundred and eight. Lira at the roof's edge: "Two hundred times. He counted." / "So do you. I've never once heard you say never."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:43:- **The board's room:** the wall rewritten, tenth; "Teague's nine up… He read that slip yesterday. Read it twice… I'd have done the same, and I told him, and he said he knew." **The council, once, in order:** Karis's case; Brom ("A survey kit's a cart's worth… That's not the reason. That's what it is."); Lira ("I'm saying it's a walk and a carry. I'm not saying it isn't the other thing."); Cael: "It pays."; **Seln reads the paper, not the words**: "Somebody wrote this who learned to write inside." / "It goes in." / "That's not a reason not to go." **The ninety-third**: nobody says *bring her*, and Karis writes "Thornwater, ninety-third. The healer." The Part-1 summary log (protected, "Twelve weeks").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:45:- **Thornwater, day 93:** Oryn on the bench at the gate with a carter's hand; "Fifteen days. Since the break." / "Breath stops at it." / "Ninth day. I said nine. You've counted." Her **two reasons** (a patient whole and still for the long reading; the carters' claim about a healer's hands, never checked); "You're a stop. I've added you… Don't make it a long stop." Her table that evening, seen from the loft door.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:46:- **Days 94–95, six on the Fallow road** (Oryn on the mule's down-slope side; the registry sheet goes back into the box at the east gate; past Thornwater's fork the printed sheet is white). **The rise:** he looks at the dark place where an Arbiter would be. Lira's hand up: "It's like the air got thick." Brom: "Like a door closing behind me." Oryn's hands half-raised and silent. Karis: "My Arbiter's gone." Seln: "Back up. Ten paces. Tell me when it comes back." Five *backs* at one stride. The stone. **Cael felt nothing, either way, and says nothing**, for two reasons: he doesn't know what it means, and nobody asked. The log at the stone (protected). Camp on the road, no fire. The floor takes the last light like water, and Oryn holds her hands over the line until it's gone.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:47:- **Day 96, the perimeter (≈4,000, measured set piece):** procedure said once (Lira the instrument a stride inside; Karis on the line with the cord; Brom marking; Seln ahead; Oryn at the stone; Cael writing counts). The bend in Karis's wrist; **iron at the third cord**; sixty-two cords and twenty strides; ten cords to the middle; "A circle is a made shape." said once as geometry and not followed. **The stake**: registry stamp, thirty-one, a boot's width on the line, "Five years in the weather. A cold term either side."; "You drive them where you've measured to." [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2; restates protected Ch10 — OWNER-pending #48]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:48:- **The trials at the stone:** Lira's full burst becomes a step ("It's in me. It's not in the air."; the clock line); Brom's "Skin."; Karis sees every point and can fill none ("It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend."); Seln vanishes for a breath without his Path ("It was never most of what I do."); **Oryn's three crossings** with Brom's arm in her hands ("Nothing in my hands" / "A healer's hands stop working there."). **Cael's two private tests:** the Iron read released before the stride, running across it; at twenty strides a foot's worth of Wind evasion round a stone. From behind it is a man stepping. "It was dark before. It's dark now." Both halves true; together not the truth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:49:- **Six over; the site catalogued** (eleven uprights broken at eleven heights; floor twenty-six strides; level under the cord; seamless under his palms, written only as "no seam"; the lip; Karis's chips don't match; the bands "None I own…"). **No instruments anywhere.** **The den** under the far lip (fresh prints; bones in one clause; scat; a hollow worn smooth). "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight." Everyone looks at the line and the sun, then at Oryn, then at him. The log at the far lip (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:56:- Oryn reads nobody inside. She has now crossed (with Brom and with the six); her eight solo crossings are M5's.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:57:- No stillhound is seen; it is all sign. The movement ends at dusk at the far lip, about to move.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:62:The six-day road's incidents; the plank and the room; how the letters land; the void road's country; Thornwater's evening; the order and texture of the trials; the site's light; Teague's and Karis's windows.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. Thornwater's people stay unnamed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈34,000. **Seln cutaway ≈2,000** (day 97, at the stone through the night and then at the stake: the drawer in his memory opening on maps with holes; it ends as he asks for the carter's map; he does not know, and never learns, where the file is). **Lira cutaway ≈2,000** (days 97–98: one arm across her chest, the order, "Later" kept on her side; walking flat-footed because Oryn said).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:19:> - **Bodies at dusk:** Cael's ribs remain taped until day 99 and his calf remains bound, not mended; Lira's tibia is new and barred from running until about day 110, her ankle remains unmended/taped, and she has drawn her knife; Brom's wrist is sound; Karis is three parts full; Seln is unmarked; Oryn cannot read or mend inside (`manuscript/chapter-29.md:23-43,181-233`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:207-215,237`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:169-179`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:21:> - **Live Arbiter result:** Karis, Brom, Seln, Lira and Oryn fail at the same step; Cael's Arbiter was already dark and remains described only that way. Oryn knows no fragment mechanism (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:189-229`; `manuscript/chapter-29.md:181-233,283-297`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:23:> - **Exact party/object placement:** six at the den; Brom wears the middle box; Seln is on one knee; Oryn's mule is hobbled west of the line stone with two panniers, six borrowed blankets, the unused left boot and covered crossbow; two boxes remain in Thornwater, with the reserve sealed in the third (`manuscript/chapter-27.md:13-29`; `manuscript/chapter-30.md:3-7,219-239`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:167,183`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:25:> - **Maps and withheld memory:** Karis's calfskin has three circles, two marked *guess*; the registry sheet has seven dashed roads and the Fallow is the third. Seln has not yet supplied his map-memory inference; that remains M5's (`manuscript/chapter-26.md:109-149`; `MOVEMENT-004.md:54-56`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:25-26`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:26:> - **Accounts/open obligations:** 108 marks in hand; one sixty-yard four-strand rope owed in kind; the two HOLD slips remain unresolved; the Fallow hundred remains lodged against the broker's mark (`manuscript/chapter-24.md:3-21,227-245`; `manuscript/chapter-25.md:229-253`; `AUTHOR-REPORT.md:181-185`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:28:> - **Oryn's route choice:** she replaced four extra table days plus the added deep-reading day with this road, explicitly owing Thornwater's short bench on return; she has been round the Ring by the ruts thirty times but had never crossed (`manuscript/chapter-22.md:223-231`; `manuscript/chapter-26.md:195-215`; `manuscript/chapter-27.md:249-253`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:43:- **The Ring (≈8,000–9,500 across two chapters), a retreat with a geometry.** The line is the objective. Nine counted on the white. "The road's cut." / "The grass. Where the cord went." Brom holds the lip: a hand's-height drop that robs a hound of drive, the haft, a man the pack cannot hear. Lira runs the rim's turned edge; the ankle goes a third time; the forearm taken and held; she cannot burst it off. **Brom's bolt through the eye at thirteen feet.** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] Oryn's hands: "Nothing… Nothing in my hands." Cloth and knees. "Move. I can't fix this here. Move." Brom's string opens his fingers in the dark. The lane counted down, 160 to 60, the scrub moving at Lira's pace and never showing a shape. They are *careless* in here, because no prey has ever shouted. **Karis down at sixty**, hands on a throat, the jaws closing across her fists, the loudest sound on the ring. **Shadow, once, ten strides**. Only Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln have the sightline; Oryn is screened by Brom and fixed on Lira/Karis, sees no discontinuity and cannot attribute the movement. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B2] The throw. Then *he stops holding*: Wind full, north off the lane; every head turns; then everything, one after another, so there is never a breath when he is not the loudest thing on the floor. Pressure for noise; Ember held out; Blade ringing with nothing to cut; Storm seeding the rut, the Iron/body read already released to the air and unavailable under his soles until the lane is relinquished [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B3]; Anchor off its hold and looking west. North to the rut, **east the wrong way** about a hundred and thirty yards, back west. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] Seln's "Back" from the stone and Lira's a breath after. The second lock with Compression at contact. Over the stone. **The bolt at six feet.** [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2] From within ten feet, Anchor's perception sees Karis's points before they light [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B1]: **the wall of ignition along the line's inside edge**, from her knees, voiceless. Seven break out north and south along the outside; two dead. Win-sentence and costs on the page. The opponent learned nothing it could use, because it had never needed to.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:44:- **The hour's mending at the line by lantern:** "There. Back." (she does not mention the clock). The state, said because a thing not said is not a finding. **The order (protected, exact)** and the sling; "One arm. From here to the snow."; "The ankle's a tape and a season…"; Oryn flat on the road. Karis's written lines. Seln: "Nothing." Brom: "Hand." / "Morning. Wash it. I've nothing tonight." The log, including **the Book 9 plant line, exactly.** Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes." / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:45:- **The camp at the stone (night of the 96th → dawn of the 98th):** the unfiled entry (protected). Morning arithmetic aloud: Karis's throat ("Days. Hoarse before it's anything."); Brom's hand ("String… That's two."); **Cael's calf read and not mended**, the fourth failure ("I don't say a finding four times to a patient and change it on the fifth."). Oryn against the stake: "Three in two days… That's a route." The route's far end, eleven days north. **Seln at the stake**: the charcoal circle from memory lies on the carter's circle; "Ignorance doesn't stamp iron."; "The Compact knows what quiet ground does. And it's filed somewhere we can't reach." (once); "No… I carried the maps. I never saw the file." Karis: *Where*, then *Entered as said*, then *Blank. Stamped. Filed.* **The contract re-read:** a question, not a recovery; "We just told them."; "Six is wrong. I'm a stop." / "They'll write six." The dead hound dragged off and the bolt cut out (five in the sleeve); rations in sixths; nobody says *yours*. Second-night log. **Dawn of the 98th: Oryn's eight crossings alone.** He watches and does not write it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:46:- **Two days back (98–99):** Lira walking flat-footed as she is told; the calf closing with no count on the flat by the second noon. **Thornwater:** "Six. Well." Tape off in the yard ("Twenty-one days. A rib is six weeks. These are done."). The calf closed in four days. "Still and whole." / "You don't get a yes. You get told." / "What does helping look like?" / "I'll know."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:52:- Five witnesses to the Shadow use at the Ring and no one else: Oryn is at the Ring but is screened and cannot see or attribute it. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator ruling] The pack is not a witness. Shadow is used **once**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:56:- Oryn does not know the mechanism when the movement ends. The telling is M6's first scene.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:20:It is the 270th day at Lowmarch. There are six now, with Oryn's first post-thaw stop [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 20] at Pike's plank. Lira has two arms she does not quite trust, and Brom's shoulder is still bound and unread. The ferryman says the ice will go in a week, and has said so for a week. Karis's case is made and no one has answered it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:27:- **The week before the ferry** (270th–276th). Tents return to the meadow. Oryn's patients come to the plank, seen from outside. Teague's crew gets ready for the road after the thaw. [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: amendment 20]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:30:- **The plank.** Pike: "What'd he do?" / "Nothing. Out here. Nothing yet." / "Then he's nothing yet." A copper and a half for bread. Teague reads the man's hands a step longer than a crew looks. Lira's face for men in grey doesn't fit a brown coat.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:31:- **The long table** (midday). The Seln–Vastin doorway exchange, verbatim; these are their first words to each other. Vastin says the short thing: he resigned or walked out. Brom: "Three hundred miles is a demonstration." The layer: Karis supplies its existence ("Under every station on the continent. I said so at a table before we left Ostrand") [B7-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]. Vastin's new fact: "Not *will not*. *Cannot.* There is no key." The name is a citation to a designer, and the trail ends at Treswick. Vastin then has nothing to do. Lira asks "Why us." Oryn notices the knee: "Then I still haven't asked." "What follows you": nothing that crosses the Line, and the Stair's rim "is not mine". Cael remembers the Book 6 sentence and says only, "Ask him the thing you want to ask him." Karis asks. **Close (verbatim).**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:41:**Development:** about 12 Cael beats. Supporting: Vastin 3, Karis 2, Seln 1–2, Brom 1, Lira 2, Oryn 1, Pike 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:55:What the week's tents and patients look like. How the landing in flood goes. What Teague's crew does about the stranger. The order of who sits down at the long table, though Lira sits last. How the back room's lamp moves. The texture of Vastin's coat, stick and knee. Humour at the edges: Brom's pricing, Pike's ledger, the mule's empty chair.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md:157:Pike was under his sailcloth. His eyes came up as the cold came in, and went over the five in the doorway, and went over them again.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md:171:"So I'd heard." Pike dipped his pen, and wrote, and blew on it. In the last column, where a price went, he set down three things with a stop between each, and read them out as he made them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md:183:"It's first snow," said Pike. "I rule every heading off at first snow. A crew gets its season said, the once, in a line, and a number set against the line; and the number's what I carry over to the new cloth at the thaw. I've done forty today. This is the last."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md:191:Pike had his pen over the end of the line, where a figure went.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md:199:"Teague says you need a column I don't have. I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md:211:By the fire one of the two carters had tipped his head back, to look at the sailcloth over Pike's bench. Five names stood there on the eleventh line, as they had for seventeen days.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md:227:It was the third time that he had given that man the word. Teague nodded, by the width of a finger, and went back to his bench. The boy who sat there had stopped with a heel of bread half way to his mouth. He did not start again until his captain was down.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md:233:Pike had heard, and he scratched the stump of his arm through its pinned sleeve.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-59.md:235:"Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the cold road," he said, to the fire, in the size of voice that he kept for things nobody had asked him. "It's the long one, east, with the axe-head on its gate. He'd a day's posts still to set when he went off after you, and there's the whole far side to mend before the thaw. A hold will feed a crew that's mending its fence."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:8:- Owner names: no new names. The hood in the tail stays faceless. The hold child in Oryn's cutaway stays unnamed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:15:  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §2 items 23–26; §3 A (the tail), B 5; §5 (the Vastin and Oryn cutaways); §7.1 (Rune; the instruments); **§9 (all of it)**; §10 Tier A 1–3, 10, 13, 15, 17–18 and the S13–S16 Tier C lines; **§11**; §12 C10; §13.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:35:**Cutaways (~4,500):** Vastin, ~2,000, alone after the leaf. "Aimed." His sentence stays stopped in his head too. **He does not join the leaf to the sigils, does no date arithmetic, and names no seals.** Oryn, ~2,500, at a hold on her route, where a fourteen-year-old's Kindling happens. She watches a child see a sigil nobody else can see, and thinks of a dark one. **She has not heard the leaf. Nobody dies.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:36:**Development:** about 16 Cael beats (the middle-third bump). Supporting: Lira 2, Karis 2, Cleon 2, Vastin 2, Seln 1–2, Brom 1, Oryn 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-37.md:9:"That's skin," said Oryn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-37.md:35:"There," said Oryn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-37.md:69:"You're helping," said Oryn.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-37.md:135:"Eleven years," said Oryn. "I've never had my hands in something and not known what it was."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-37.md:224:There was no fright in it. It was the question that she would have put if a patient had gone white under her on the ash at Oxhollow.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-37.md:238:Oryn looked at him for as long as it takes to draw one breath, and he could not tell what was in her face. It was not fear. It had never been that. Then the corner of her mouth went down, a very little, as it went when a patient on her table began to sit up before she had done.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:8:- Owner names: no new names. The shoulder hold's factor, the ford-keeper and Teague's crew stay by role.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:15:  - From `BOOK_MAP.md`: §2 items 27–31; §3 A, C (294th; road east); §5 (the Teague cutaway); §7.1 (Force; Rune; the still place); §10 Tier A 11, 16, 23, 25, 27 and the S17–S18 Tier C lines; §12 C2, C4; §13 (the "Noted" order; Vastin's order).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29:- **Lowmarch (297th).** Pike: *Treswick. Survey read. Bearing.* The price and outcome columns are left blank, and the season line is dated. Cael reads the line the right way up. **Teague's term and contract, verbatim:** ten on a wall's count; shares by count; the field is Teague's; the reading is Karis's. "Contract. Not more than that." / "The wall's still the wall." Cael prices it honestly: Teague is the better field captain, and the rival clock still runs.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:31:- **The grade cracked (298th morning).** Teague is at the door for the dividers, not the marks. There are three marks; the box for the first tier is ruled and never used. Cleon's list puts the kindling mark and the sheet mark in one line: "A mark is a grade." Ages by first sheet: 61, 94, 138, 206. The third-tier point falls past the fourth, in the straightedge's shadow. **Oldest-last.** "It's observation … Not what it means." **Vastin's first "Noted."** Teague: "Oldest last." / "Then that's where we're going." **The log, verbatim** (the grandmother is *Cael's*: §12 C4).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:32:- **Millrace (298th evening).** "Eleven off the ridge." / "I know." The healers exchange one look, then both look at Brom's shoulder. Vastin is ordered to stand ("Nineteen days." / "Then it's eleven more."); it is his first order taken without walking it back. Oryn restates her terms: three holds owed, and "a stop on my own route". "Sixth chair." / "On my terms. Which are the only kind." **She asks each patient, "May I?"** The readings: Brom's shoulder; Lira's arm ("You listened when it told you the second time." / "Once." / "Once is once more than I priced"); Karis's hand ("Who sewed this."); the knee ("It held in a cut"; "Noted" / "That's new." / "It's a useful word." / "It's his.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:33:- **The deep reading (~3,000).** "May I?" / "Yes." It is the long one. Her current goes round the place. **The twelfth turns inward unbidden: *still*, then *set*.** It is not named, and he keeps the check out of his wrist and the change out of his face. The eyes pay in the dark. **Oryn's finding, verbatim.** He withholds his own and enters his reasons in order. Lira offers the leaf. "Is it a finding?" / "It's a leaf …" / "Then it's not mine … Tell me on the road, if there's road. Not at my table."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:36:**Physical challenge:** the road and the cut walked again on a bad knee. Force seen. As a learning encounter, the two crews work together in the Lowmarch meadow, **silent movement and march order only. They do not drill under a wall** (§13).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:37:**Cutaway (~2,500):** Teague. He sets the contract's terms before the plank, and thinks about why he is going (to be at the front of the thing). The wrist. The young one. **He knows nothing of the mechanism.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:38:**Development:** about 14 Cael beats. Supporting: Karis 2, Oryn 2, Vastin 2, Teague 2, Lira 1, Brom 1, the young one 1, Pike 1.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:43:- The Rune finding is **told to no one**. Oryn's finding is hers, whole. The two instruments' disagreement stays unresolved.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:44:- Oryn does **not** hear the leaf. Cleon is not above ground; his goodbye is at the iron door.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:46:- "Noted" order: Vastin's first is here. Teague does not say it yet.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:47:- The wall's count is the crew's six, Karis included, plus Teague's four. The healers are not on it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-08-before-the-paths/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:51:How the road east reads in reverse. The plank room's crowd. The meadow's details. Teague's crew at the table. How the grade's numbers come off the sheets. Millrace's lean-to, light and noise. How long the deep reading takes on the page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:27:There was one other man in the meadow who had not gone back to his fire. The Thornwater carter had loaded yesterday, forty sacks under a net, and he had been buckling a trace when the mule came by him. He stood now with the leather hanging from his fist, and he was looking at the boy's back as a man looks at a door behind which somebody is ill.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:29:The inn door opened, and Pike came out in his shirt.

