+## Closing mechanical audit
+
+- All 15 chapter files have balanced straight quotation marks in every paragraph, even asterisk counts, and no curly quotation marks.
+- Every `---` break has one blank line before and after. No fenced block or square-bracketed form occurs in chapters 16–30.
+- The only Arabic numerals in body text are the visible pencil note `water at 36` (ch26:115) and Karis's visible notebook entry `95th` (ch28:55). Chapter-heading numerals are metadata. All narrative counts and measurements are words.
+- The doubled-word sweep returned only grammatical perfect constructions (`had had`), not accidental duplicates.
+- The one lower-case paragraph opening is Pike's deliberately separate italic ledger continuation, `less six, the cart.` (ch24:95), already introduced as four written words beneath the prior line.
+- Two flattened paragraphs exceed 700 characters: ch23:53 (865) and ch23:127 (750). Both are complete and can be split at sentence boundaries by `fpaudio.py`.
+- No required or optional line fix emerged from the full read or the supplementary sweeps.

